    description: "Source: deep-20260407-030917 prometheus reflect agent. The LOW_DATAFLOW_SLICE_RATIO WARN at 6.0% is a measurement artifact: slice.0 grew from ~962 to 1689 nodes after the INV-kunam route resolver fix added reach into web/api/v1/api.go, dropping the dataflow/regular ratio from 6.3% to 6.0% even though both numerator and denominator grew. The underlying access_mode-annotated call-edge coverage on slice.0 is actually 53.0% and 62.0% repo-wide. Fix options: (a) decompose the signal into access_mode_edge_coverage (annotatable edges with access_mode set / total annotatable edges) and dataflow_slice_relative_size as separate metrics, (b) make the warn delta-aware (only fire when dataflow node count drops absolutely, not when ratio drops because of denominator growth), (c) drop the ratio metric entirely in favor of (a). The current single-ratio metric will continue to false-alarm whenever a quality fix elsewhere in the pipeline grows the regular slice."  # 13be
    fields: {}  # 13be
